{"step_index":943,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:28:55Z","thinking":"**Exploring Locking Mechanisms**\n\nI've been investigating file locking on macOS, realizing `flock` isn't readily available. I'm now looking at alternatives. `shlock`, `python-filelock`, or even an atomic `mkdir` approach seem viable. I'm currently leaning towards checking out the python methods, like `python3 -c \"import fcntl...\"`\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Add fcntl lock to agent_speak.sh to prevent overlapping audio and audio cutoffs\"","EndLine":"39","Instruction":"\"Wrap voice playback with python fcntl.flock to serialize CoreAudio speech output across all agents\"","ReplacementContent":"\"VOICE=\\\"Jamie (Premium)\\\"\\n\\ncase \\\"$AGENT\\\" in\\n  maxx|bm_george)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Evan (Enhanced)\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  jarvis|am_adam)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Jamie (Premium)\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  daxx)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Lee (Premium)\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  clara|af_sarah)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Zoe (Premium)\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  vance|am_michael)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Nathan (Enhanced)\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n    VOICE=\\\"Jamie (Premium)\\\"\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport sys, subprocess, fcntl\\n\\nvoice = sys.argv[1]\\ntext = sys.argv[2]\\n\\nwith open('/tmp/coreaudio_single_speaker.lock', 'w') as lockfile:\\n    fcntl.flock(lockfile.fileno(), fcntl.LOCK_EX)\\n    try:\\n        subprocess.run(['say', '-v', voice, text], check=True)\\n    finally:\\n        fcntl.flock(lockfile.fileno(), fcntl.LOCK_UN)\\n\\\" \\\"$VOICE\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n\"","StartLine":"19","TargetContent":"\"case \\\"$AGENT\\\" in\\n  maxx|bm_george)\\n    say -v \\\"Evan (Enhanced)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  jarvis|am_adam)\\n    say -v \\\"Jamie (Premium)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  daxx)\\n    say -v \\\"Lee (Premium)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  clara|af_sarah)\\n    say -v \\\"Zoe (Premium)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  vance|am_michael)\\n    say -v \\\"Nathan (Enhanced)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n    say -v \\\"Jamie (Premium)\\\" \\\"$RAW_TEXT\\\"\\n    ;;\\nesac\"","TargetFile":"\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh\"","toolAction":"\"Adding fcntl mutex lock to agent_speak.sh\"","toolSummary":"\"Audio serialization lock implementation\""}}]}
